      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY 4.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0",
      "artist": "Dack9",
      "credit": "Own work",
      "source": "Крепость Буртанж (вид сверху)",
      "description": "Fort Bourtange is a fort in the Netherlands on the border with Germany. It was founded in 1580 during the Eighty Years' War (the Dutch struggle for independence from Spain). It protected the only road from Germany to the city of Groningen. The fortress belongs to the bastion system of fortifications, which replaced medieval knightly castles. Such bastion fortresses became popular starting in the 16th century. The high stone walls of classic medieval castles were easily destroyed by artillery, so the walls began to be built lower and thicker. The fortress towers also underwent changes: they began to be given a pentagonal, star-shaped form for more complete coverage of the space in front of them. Gradually, the size of the towers increased, and soon they turned into independent fortresses.",
      "dateCreated": "2019-12-28 14:07:59",
      "sourceType": "core",
      "sourceArticleId": "fort-bourtange-wp",
      "sourceGeohash4": "u1mj",
      "smallPath": "_m/u/1/m/j/fort-bourtange-wp/fort-bourtange-fort-ne-small.webp"
    },
